From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000006 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton <fourth@devpins.org>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: usb-audio: tune compiler flags for the USB-DAC hot path

This device is a dedicated bit-perfect audio player feeding a Chord Mojo 2
USB DAC (beryllium / SDM845). Tighten the snd-usb-audio objects a little:
align the hot URB/PCM callbacks to a cache line and relax FP semantics the
driver never relies on.

Scoped via ccflags-y so it applies to the snd-usb-audio and snd-usbmidi-lib
objects built in sound/usb/ (sub-directory modules keep their own flags).
Only flags valid on the kernel's plain clang (LLVM=1) build are used:

  - -O2 is already the kernel default (CONFIG_CC_OPTIMIZE_FOR_PERFORMANCE);
    -O3 is intentionally avoided as it can reorder URB-submission callbacks.
  - -mllvm -polly=... is omitted: Polly is a Qualcomm CPULLVM feature, not
    enabled in this toolchain, so passing it can fail the build.
  - the machine scheduler is already enabled by default for AArch64.

Net effect is small; the substantive low-latency wins (RT IRQ threads,
nrpacks=1, performance governor, autosuspend off, lowlatency=1) are applied
at runtime/config. Zero-risk micro-optimisation.

Signed-off-by: Anton <fourth@devpins.org>
---
 sound/usb/Makefile | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/usb/Makefile b/sound/usb/Makefile
--- a/sound/usb/Makefile
+++ b/sound/usb/Makefile
@@ -3,6 +3,13 @@
 # Makefile for ALSA
 #
 
+# Audiophile tuning for the bit-perfect USB-DAC player (beryllium/SDM845 + Mojo 2):
+# tighten icache alignment of the snd-usb-audio hot callbacks and relax FP semantics.
+# Kept to flags valid on the kernel's plain clang (LLVM=1) build. -O2 is already the
+# kernel default (CONFIG_CC_OPTIMIZE_FOR_PERFORMANCE); -mllvm -polly=... is omitted
+# (Polly is a Qualcomm CPULLVM feature, not in this toolchain).
+ccflags-y += -falign-functions=32 -fno-math-errno -fno-trapping-math
+
 snd-usb-audio-y := 	card.o \
 			clock.o \
 			endpoint.o \
--
